Network Administration Lab
Project Overview

This project documents practical networking and troubleshooting exercises designed to develop and demonstrate network administration skills.

The laboratory environment simulates a small business network containing servers, client computers, networking equipment, and shared network resources.

The project focuses on IP addressing, DNS, DHCP, connectivity, network troubleshooting, and basic network infrastructure management.

Project Objectives

The objectives of this project were to:

Configure IPv4 network settings
Understand TCP/IP networking
Configure static IP addresses
Configure DHCP
Configure DNS
Test network connectivity
Troubleshoot network communication problems
Understand router and switch connectivity
Configure Windows clients for network access
Document network infrastructure
Develop practical network administration skills
